# ============================================================================
# Two trees share this repository: the retrieval experiments run on the Spark
# (src/, deploy/, RESULTS.md and the other reports) and the COMPASS pipeline
# mirror (agent/, env/, generate/, benchmark/, mcp/, tests/, build.py). The
# repository is PUBLIC. The rule that governs both halves: the survey instrument
# -- codebook CSVs, the built dictionary, and any artifact carrying question or
# option wording per row -- is never tracked. README.md lists what is withheld.
# ============================================================================

# --- environments and caches -------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- the instrument, in every form --------------------------------------------
# build/ is reproduced exactly by `python build.py` from raw/ on the training
# machine (the hash pin lives in tests/test_dictionary.py::BUILD_HASH). Neither
# is obtainable from a clone: README.md, "What is withheld". On the Spark the same
# dictionary lives at the root as dictionary.json.
build/
raw/
# ... and as symlinks: a trailing-slash pattern matches a directory, never a
# link to one, so a linked artifact would otherwise be stageable.
build
raw
*.csv
codebook.csv        # redundant under *.csv; kept as the training machine's no-read guard
dictionary.json
targets.json
# deploy/targets.json carries the stem and option wording of all 1,353 targets;
# it ships with deploy/model/ by rsync and is sha256-checked by the manifest.
deploy/targets.json
deploy/model/

# --- the answer keys, as MODULES ----------------------------------------------
# The three withheld modules named by
# `benchmark/contamination_check.py::WITHHELD_MODULES`. They hold published
# paper content -- rediscovery design anchors, prevalence rows, leak facts --
# and they exist only in the scoring clone, where `git add -A` reaches them and
# nothing stopped it. The discipline until now was UNTRACKED and nothing
# enforced it: measured 2026-09-15, `prevalence_key.py` has zero commits in the
# whole history and `leak_facts.py` has two, which is the recorded public
# exposure (`TASKS.md` §Known-open defects). An ignore entry is what turns that
# discipline into a mechanism.
#
# THIS DOES NOT UN-PUBLISH ANYTHING. `leak_facts.py` is reachable from the live
# `origin/main`; the adding commit stays an ancestor and an ignore rule says
# nothing about history. This prevents the NEXT staging, not the last one, and
# the remedy for that one is the user's (rotation, or accepting it as
# disclosed). Nor does it stop `git add -f`, which is how the tracked artifacts
# under `out/` got there.
#
# Pinned by `tests/test_code_standards.py::
# test_every_withheld_key_module_is_unstageable`, which asks git and reads the
# module list from `WITHHELD_MODULES` rather than repeating it here.
benchmark/design_key.py
benchmark/prevalence_key.py
benchmark/leak_facts.py

# --- data, model and vector artifacts -----------------------------------------
*.json
*.jsonl
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
!.claude/**/*.json
!curated/**/*.json
# the small, wording-free half of the deploy bundle travels in git so a clone
# can self-verify (deploy/smoke_test.py step 0)
!deploy/manifest.json
!deploy/target_vectors.safetensors
# the page's artifacts, without which `GET /` renders empty panels. They are
# generated FROM the instrument but carry none of it: `site/tools/
# no_instrument.py` forbids any five-word run shared with a dictionary entry and
# any variable key, and passed over all of site/ on 2026-09-15 (exit 0, 9,424
# runs and 5,608 keys checked). That gate is the reason these may be tracked.
!site/artifacts/*.json
# out/ and run/ are ignored wholesale; the handful of tracked artifacts under
# out/ were force-added (git add -f) after a wording scan. See README.md.
out/
runs/
run/
runs
run
*.log
parked/
fixtures/
parked
fixtures
benchmark/fixtures
# the one fixture that carries no instrument wording: hand-authored template
# fields for the 44 negative requests
!fixtures/negative_expansion_fields.json

